---

<section id="architecture">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-tag">03 · COMPUTER ARCHITECTURE</div>

    <h1 class="section-title">Computer Architecture Concept</h1>

    <p class="section-description">
      The Apollo Guidance Computer (AGC) guided and controlled the Apollo 11
      Lunar Module Eagle during its descent to the Moon. Using only a 2.048 MHz
      processor, 4 KB of RAM, and 72 KB of ROM, its software architecture
      enabled reliable real-time operation despite the severe hardware
      limitations of the 1960s.
      <strong
        >To explore the AGC's architecture, click any of the <span
          class="text-gold">yellow nodes</span
        >.</strong
      >
    </p>

    <Chip client:load />
  </div>
</section>
